<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · ideology</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islamism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1922 CE – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Islamism is a range of movements holding that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> should shape politics and the state through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a>. Formed by Rashid Rida, Hassan al-Banna, Maududi and Qutb after the end of the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>, it took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in 1979 and entered elections across the Muslim world, while militant Salafi jihadists from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> to ISIL waged armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>; since about 2020 observers have seen it decline.</p></div>
